  "rubric_items": [
    {"id": "DS-R1", "score": 5, "reason": "Builds on the existing PatientRepo/PatientService layering, the HMS-1 NextAppointment type, dateTime/useSettings and the existing routes. No new infrastructure and no migration."},
    {"id": "DS-R2", "score": 5, "reason": "S-1..S-4 are each mapped to components. Strict &gt; now covers S-2 AC3. Using this.clock() per request covers S-1 AC4. The dateTime link covers S-1 AC2/AC3 and S-3. The table and the Book appointment button are untouched for S-4."},
    {"id": "DS-R3", "score": 5, "reason": "Every new field on EP-1..EP-3 has a name, type, nullability, format and example. The null condition is precise enough to test."},
    {"id": "DS-R4", "score": 4, "reason": "Every choice is cited or decided by A-03/A-04, and all 23 claims check out. One gap: CO-1 leaves open how list uses the extracted query, but it is still marked known."},
    {"id": "DS-R5", "score": 5, "reason": "Explains the trade-offs for server vs client, snake_case naming and skipping a migration. The 'indexed lookup' claim holds: appointment_patient_start_idx exists."},
    {"id": "DS-R6", "score": 4, "reason": "Clear and well structured, but the Overview and CO-1 describe the list refactor differently."}
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F-1",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "consistency",
      "text": "The Overview says list and get both call PatientRepo.nextAppointment(id, now), but CO-1 says list may instead keep its one-query-per-page form. Calling a per-id method from list would break HMS-1's one query per page (an N+1 query). The design does not pick an option.",
      "cites": [
        {"ref": "artifacts/HMS-15/run_01M7HYHSSG24BWQN7R2M4AZRF3/design.md#L173", "quote": "moves into a shared `PatientRepo.nextAppointment(id, now)`, which both `list` and `get` call"},
        {"ref": "artifacts/HMS-15/run_01M7HYHSSG24BWQN7R2M4AZRF3/design.md#L187", "quote": "`list` keeps its one-query-per-page form or calls the same SQL fragment"},
        {"ref": "sample-system:api/src/repositories/patientRepo.ts#L100", "quote": "earliest Scheduled appointment starting after `now`, in one query per page"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Pick one approach: share a SQL fragment (status, &gt; now, ORDER BY starts_at, id LIMIT 1) used by the list's lateral join and by nextAppointment(id, now), so list stays one query per page. Then make the Overview match."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-2",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "completeness",
      "text": "PatientRepo.get returns Omit&lt;PatientDetail, 'appointments'&gt;. Once CO-3 adds next_appointment to PatientDetail, repo.get's return type must also omit next_appointment, or it will fail to type-check. CO-1/CO-3 do not mention this.",
      "cites": [
        {"ref": "sample-system:api/src/repositories/patientRepo.ts#L148", "quote": "Promise&lt;Omit&lt;PatientDetail, 'appointments'&gt; | null&gt;"},
        {"ref": "artifacts/HMS-15/run_01M7HYHSSG24BWQN7R2M4AZRF3/design.md#L189", "quote": "add `next_appointment: NextAppointment | null`"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "In CO-1, note that repo.get's return type becomes Omit&lt;PatientDetail, 'appointments' | 'next_appointment'&gt;."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-3",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "correctness",
      "text": "PatientService.get calls this.clock() separately (inside today() and for appointments). The design's promise to use 'the same this.clock() instant' means reading the clock once into a local now. The current code does not do that yet.",
      "cites": [
        {"ref": "sample-system:api/src/services/patientService.ts#L42", "quote": "appointments: await repo.appointments(id, this.clock())"},
        {"ref": "artifacts/HMS-15/run_01M7HYHSSG24BWQN7R2M4AZRF3/design.md#L188", "quote": "using the same `this.clock()` value as `appointments`"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "In CO-2, state: const now = this.clock(); pass now to both appointments and nextAppointment."
    }
  ],
